Likutay Halachos &middot; Yoreh De&apos;ah, Part Two

Laws of Chalah

Hilchos Chalah

&middot; &middot; &#10022; &middot; &middot;

Halacha Four

Part One &mdash; Sections &#x05D0;&ndash;&#x05D5;

Section Five &middot; &#x05D4;

And therefore the commandment of Chalah is practiced even in this time, even outside the Land of Israel &mdash; so that the Torah of Chalah not be forgotten from Israel. Which is not the case with Terumos and Ma&rsquo;asros which are not practiced outside the Land of Israel at all. For Chalah &mdash; because it comes at the end of the completion of the bread, when then is the essential revelation of the Will that illuminates at the time of eating as mentioned, which is the essential rectification of all the sparks, which is the essential rectification of the exile as mentioned &mdash; therefore it is practiced even now outside the Land of Israel, so that the Torah of Chalah not be forgotten from Israel. So that we merit even now with the commandment of Chalah &mdash; that is: even though we are so subdued in exile, nonetheless we must strengthen ourselves in faith in Hashem blessed-be-He, and know that Hashem blessed-be-He is still with us and beside us etc., and the Will is still free (haratzon chofshi). And we can strengthen ourselves until we merit the illumination of the Will, through which we clarify all the clarifications and the redemption comes in general and in particular, and it will be fulfilled: &ldquo;and he shall remain also to our G-d&rdquo; &mdash; as mentioned. All of which is merited through the commandment of Chalah by separating the firstfruits (raishis) for the Kohen who is composed of ben v&rsquo;talmid, through which one merits the illumination of the Will etc. as mentioned.

Section Six &middot; &#x05D5;

And therefore the measure (shi&rsquo;ur) of the commandment of Chalah is forty-three eggs (mem-gimel baitzim) &mdash; which is the aspect of gam [also] &mdash; the aspect of &ldquo;v&rsquo;af gam zos bihyosam b&rsquo;eretz oyevayhem lo me&rsquo;astim&rdquo; [and even this: when they are in the land of their enemies, I did not despise them] etc. (Vayikra 26:44). That is: even though Israel are in the land of their enemies, in places very far from holiness, and they are subdued there in exile in very great exile &mdash; nonetheless: &ldquo;I did not despise them and I did not abhor them to destroy them, heaven forbid, for I am Hashem their G-d.&rdquo; For I reveal to them that Hashem is still with them etc. And through this they raise all the distant places to holiness, in the aspect of &ldquo;and he shall remain also to our G-d.&rdquo; And this is the aspect of Chalah whose measure is forty-three eggs &mdash; the aspect of gam mentioned &mdash; the aspects of &ldquo;v&rsquo;af gam zos&rdquo; etc., the aspects of &ldquo;v&rsquo;nish&rsquo;ar gam hu le&rsquo;Elokaynu&rdquo; as mentioned.

